\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-7A+8I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-7A+8I) & =O \\\\ A-7I+8{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{7}{8}I-\\frac{1}{8}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{7}{8},$ $q=-\\frac{1}{8}$ and\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{7}{8}+(-\\frac{1}{8})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354448 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186353838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354448 #edb/ref 1069 "q-85931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354448 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354448 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354448 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62f9e5ba-0775-5b99-88ac-c3c5c53cda55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354448 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-x-20\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"9\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\phantom{|}\\,\\,}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"