 =q(x)p(x)+(2x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{10}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(2A-3I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(2A-3I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(2A-3I) \\\\  & =2A-3I \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186392153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186392151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392148 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5a7442f8-2e08-50f7-921a-87fb338cdbdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392149 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -16\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392149 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392149 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "33d95a80-3f16-57c4-aa0e-d7a0b263509f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392150 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -24 \\\\ 8 & -16\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186392150 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392150 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7ade6fcc-fefb-5c26-9596-732bb7e6456e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186392151 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{bmatri